   "texts_sent": [
    "In February twenty twenty-six, the average thirty-year fixed mortgage rate in the U.S. fell to five point nine eight percent, the lowest since September twenty twenty-two.",
    "Nora had borrowed in twenty twenty-three, at seven point six two percent.",
    "At the February rate, a new loan would have cut her payment by four hundred fifty-nine dollars a month.",
    "She didn't take it.",
    "By late September, the rate was back above seven percent, for the first time since January twenty twenty-five.",
    "Now a letter comes from her lender: an offer to refinance, a new loan at a slightly lower rate that pays off the old one, for five thousand one hundred twenty-four dollars in fees.",
    "How big a rate cut makes that worth it for Nora — and where would your own loan fall?",
    "And why would a smaller mortgage need a bigger cut?",
    "By month twenty-four, she owes one thousand one hundred thirty-three dollars more than if she had kept the old loan.",
    "If she sold the house then, that one thousand one hundred thirty-three dollars would come out of her sale money, so it cancels part of what she has saved.",
    "Her savings need a few more months to cover it, and the gap keeps growing a little while they do.",
    "Count it, and break-even moves from month twenty-four to month thirty."
   ],
